  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "The wish also travels to the past",
     "texto": [
      "If the wish is from **today**, the verb goes in the present subjunctive:\n\n- **Quiero** que **vengas**.\n\nIf the wish is from **yesterday**, both verbs go in the past:\n\n- **Quería** que **vinieras**.\n- Me **pidió** que **llamara**.\n\nThe second form is the **imperfect subjunctive**. It is used when the person changes: the one who wishes and the one who acts are different."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "gramatica",
     "titulo": "How the imperfect subjunctive is formed",
     "texto": [
      "Start from the **ellos** form of the preterite, drop **-ron** and add **-ra, -ras, -ra, -ramos, -rais, -ran**:\n\n- hablaron → hablara, hablaras, hablara, habláramos, hablarais, hablaran\n- vinieron → viniera, vinieras, viniera, viniéramos, vinierais, vinieran\n- pidieron → pidiera, pidieras, pidiera, pidiéramos, pidierais, pidieran\n\nThe rule of two persons:\n\n- Same subject → **infinitive**: Quería ir.\n- Different subject → **que + imperfect subjunctive**: Quería que vinieras.\n\nThe present turns into the past: quiero que **vengas** → quería que **vinieras**."
     ],
     "ejemplos": [
